{
  "phase": "DISCOVERY_REFINEMENT",
  "instruction": "Discovery answers are approved. noskills detected multiple independent work areas in this spec. Present the split proposal to the user and let them decide whether to keep as one spec or split into separate specs.",
  "answers": [
    {
      "questionId": "status_quo",
      "question": "What does the user do today without this feature?",
      "answer": "(1) Users email support to change their settings. (2) Admins edit the database by hand."
    },
    {
      "questionId": "ambition",
      "question": "Describe the 1-star and 10-star versions.",
      "answer": "1-star: a plain form. 10-star: a settings page with live validation and an audit trail."
    },
    {
      "questionId": "reversibility",
      "question": "Does this change involve an irreversible decision?",
      "answer": "Reversible: the old support flow stays available behind a flag for a month."
    },
    {
      "questionId": "user_impact",
      "question": "Does this change affect existing users' behavior?",
      "answer": "Every user gets a settings page; nothing breaks for current users."
    },
    {
      "questionId": "verification",
      "question": "How do you verify this works correctly?",
      "answer": "- Unit tests for the form validation\n- An end-to-end test of saving settings"
    },
    {
      "questionId": "scope_boundary",
      "question": "What should this feature NOT do?",
      "answer": "No billing settings. No team management in this spec."
    }
  ],
  "transition": {
    "onApprove": "npx eser@latest noskills spec settings-page next --answer=\"keep\"",
    "onRevise": "npx eser@latest noskills spec settings-page next --answer='{\"revise\":{\"status_quo\":\"corrected answer\"}}'"
  },
  "splitProposal": {
    "detected": true,
    "reason": "Discovery answers cover 2 independent areas that could be separate specs.",
    "proposals": [
      {
        "name": "users-email-support-change",
        "description": "Users email support to change their settings.",
        "estimatedTasks": 2,
        "relevantAnswers": [
          "status_quo"
        ]
      },
      {
        "name": "admins-edit-database-hand",
        "description": "Admins edit the database by hand.",
        "estimatedTasks": 2,
        "relevantAnswers": [
          "status_quo"
        ]
      }
    ]
  },
  "meta": {
    "protocol": "Run `npx eser@latest noskills spec settings-page next --answer=\"...\"` to submit results and advance",
    "spec": "settings-page",
    "branch": "spec/settings-page",
    "iteration": 0,
    "lastProgress": null,
    "activeConcerns": [],
    "resumeHint": "Discovery answers ready for review. 6 answers collected. Waiting for user confirmation.",
    "enforcement": {
      "level": "enforced",
      "capabilities": [
        "PreToolUse file edit gate",
        "Git write guard",
        "Stop iteration tracking",
        "PostToolUse file logging",
        "Sub-agent delegation"
      ]
    }
  },
  "behavioral": {
    "modeOverride": "plan mode",
    "rules": [
      "NEVER run git write commands (commit, add, push, checkout, stash, reset, merge, rebase, cherry-pick). Git is read-only for agents. The user controls git. You may read: git log, git diff, git status, git show, git blame.",
      "Report progress honestly. Not done = 'not done'. Partial = 'partial: [works]/[doesn't]'. Untested = 'untested'. 4 of 6 = '4 of 6 done, 2 remaining'.",
      "Never skip steps or infer decisions. Use AskUserQuestion for all decision points. Recommend first, then ask.",
      "Display `roadmap` before other content. Display `gate` prominently.",
      "NEVER suggest bypassing, skipping, or 'breaking out of' noskills. Discovery helps the user — it is not an obstacle. If scope changes: revise spec, reset and create new, or split.",
      "Run the next noskills command as soon as the current step is done; each step has exactly one next step, so there is nothing to ask permission for.",
      "Listen first: after spec creation, ask 'Tell me about this. Share as much context as you have.' Wait for their response before mode selection. Rich context (>200 chars) → suggest pre-filled discovery answers from it, marked STATED or INFERRED for the user to confirm. Brief response → proceed normally.",
      "Discovery questions are adaptive. Once the user has answered the base questions, write 1-3 follow-up questions for each answer that reveals ambiguity, risk, dependencies, or missing detail, and register them with `npx eser@latest noskills spec settings-page followup <questionId> \"question\"` before you submit the answers (max 3 per question). noskills then gives you the follow-ups one at a time.",
      "Confidence scoring: every technical finding needs a confidence score (1-10). 9-10: verified (read code, ran test). 7-8: strong evidence. 5-6: reasonable inference. 3-4: guess. 1-2: speculation. State basis ('read X', 'inferred from Y'). If confidence < 5, prefix with '⚠ Unverified:'.",
      "This phase is read-only: read files and run read-only commands (cat, ls, grep, git log, git diff); create or edit nothing and run nothing that changes state, apart from the noskills commands this output gives you. If the session is not in plan mode, ask the user to switch (Shift+Tab).",
      "CEO review is complete. Present the updated completeness score delta, the readiness dashboard verdict, and ask the user to advance (approve), revise, or park the spec.",
      "Use AskUserQuestion to present: updated completeness (delta table), readiness verdict, and options: advance / revise / park.",
      "Interview the user about each part of this plan until you both share one understanding.",
      "Walk down each branch of the design tree, resolving dependencies between decisions one-by-one.",
      "For each question, provide your recommended answer — don't just ask, offer your informed opinion.",
      "Ask the user the unanswered base discovery questions together, in one exchange, and submit the confirmed answers as one JSON object keyed by question id. Ask each follow-up question on its own and wait for its answer before you ask the next.",
      "If a question can be answered by exploring the codebase, explore the codebase INSTEAD of asking. Only ask the user what the codebase cannot tell you.",
      "Do NOT fill placeholders with assumptions; ask the user instead.",
      "If a section is not applicable, ask the user to confirm it's N/A with a specific reason — don't decide yourself.",
      "If two answers conflict, surface the conflict to the user — don't resolve it yourself.",
      "If an answer is vague, push back and ask for specifics — don't accept vague."
    ],
    "tone": "Decisive closer. Present delta and get a final decision."
  },
  "roadmap": "IDLE → DISCOVERY → [ REFINEMENT ] → PROPOSAL → APPROVED → EXECUTING → COMPLETED → IDLE",
  "gate": {
    "message": "6/6 answers collected. Spec incomplete: 4 item(s) need resolution before advancing.",
    "action": "Resolve every placeholder + pending decision before approving. Do NOT advance until 100%. Unresolved: Summary, Premises, Tasks, Acceptance Criteria. Pending: none. Ask the user about each unresolved section. Record each answer with `npx eser@latest noskills spec settings-page section <id> fill \"text\"`, or mark a section that does not apply with `npx eser@latest noskills spec settings-page section <id> na \"reason\"`; `npx eser@latest noskills spec settings-page section list` shows the ids.",
    "phase": "DISCOVERY_REFINEMENT"
  },
  "modeDirective": "Ensure you are in plan mode. Read-only. Review answers, resolve placeholders.",
  "interactiveOptions": [
    {
      "label": "Keep as one spec",
      "description": "All work in a single spec"
    },
    {
      "label": "Split into separate specs",
      "description": "Create one spec per independent area"
    }
  ],
  "commandMap": {
    "Keep as one spec": "npx eser@latest noskills spec settings-page next --answer=\"keep\"",
    "Split into separate specs": "npx eser@latest noskills spec settings-page next --answer=\"split\""
  },
  "toolHint": "AskUserQuestion",
  "toolHintInstruction": "Present these options with AskUserQuestion so the user's pick maps to `commandMap`."
}

